  interkit - Debian + Fossil


  Welcome to interkit - a Debian server: mail, chat, relay and web admin.

  FIRST, run the guided setup (it asks for your domain, then does the rest):

        sudo interkit-setup

  New to Linux? The basics:
    ls            list files          cd DIR     go into a folder (cd .. = up)
    pwd           where am I          cat FILE   show a file
    nano FILE     edit a file (vim: quit with Esc, then :q!)
    sudo COMMAND  run as administrator (type your password; nothing shows)
    ip -br a      show this machine's IP address
    htop          what is running (q quits)    man COMMAND   manual (q quits)
    sudo reboot / sudo poweroff       Tab completes names, Up = last command

  No copy/paste on this screen? Use ssh from your own computer:
    ssh USER@THAT-IP
  Enter API keys in a browser:  sudo interkit-setup web-ui
  (or put interkit.env on a USB stick).
  Web admin (Fossil), from another computer:  http://THAT-IP:8080
    user admin, password: sudo cat /root/fossil-admin-password
  Help: interkit-setup -h
